of-coordinates matrix from the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}}$ is given above. Find $[x]_{C}$ given that $x=5{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}-{b}_{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $x=5{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}-{b}_{3},$ we have\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nGiven the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C,$ we find the coordinates of $x$ relative to $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}[\\,x\\,]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-113557/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e2a1713-45a0-5ac9-812e-efe047dbc9eb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-113557"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-82599/selection/71150bb92c2159182160731a0e81514442f0b073b4ef5e4744d8884cdad1ca31" :answer/id #uuid "9d7e3025-aa12-5a30-890f-ff82d43c3a3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82599/selection/9576b88f964aafa72109b0daf8e5011e1276983566a81ec66c0ae1d06856933c" :answer/id #uuid "1b38ee4d-7e5c-5b05-b3f7-a9698dfc2612" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82599/selection/c87615c8ca70fd83c2dbb380cf667fd8a0c153d05689ea5ad0b2b4d3b0ad2a84" :answer/id #uuid "b955ffb2-d295-5482-8f7a-75999e7c5595" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82599/selection/b8b1dee7baf8d854ae4d8a7d6f5fab2688cd2796a15b0eba7bf650f83d3ca87d" :answer/id #uuid "2a72c860-b475-5696-881b-d0eebcd791c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82599/selection/ed3e5772ada91df6851b168e6a1c19726b0e2e4ebaec70bec9c0dc7fa837322a" :answer/id #uuid "2e7f03a1-be68-52a4-8ff5-b3bf0003e488" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82599/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed7ca470-5057-53c7-9e21-43e1ca183d27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-82599/selection/71150bb92c2159182160731a0e81514442f0b073b4ef5e4744d8884cdad1ca31" :answer-field/choices ["q-82599/selection/71150bb92c2159182160731a0e81514442f0b073b4ef5e4744d8884cdad1ca31" "q-82599/selection/9576b88f964aafa72109b0daf8e5011e1276983566a81ec66c0ae1d06856933c" "q-82599/selection/c87615c8ca70fd83c2dbb380cf667fd8a0c153d05689ea5ad0b2b4d3b0ad2a84" "q-82599/selection/b8b1dee7baf8d854ae4d8a7d6f5fab2688cd2796a15b0eba7bf650f83d3ca87d" "q-82599/selection/ed3e5772ada91df6851b168e6a1c19726b0e2e4ebaec70bec9c0dc7fa837322a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-82599" :question/id #uuid "50e979ba-7b97-5986-8a48-8c9960bb8901" :question/math-academy-id "q-82599" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ to $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ is given below. Find $[x]_{B}$ given that $x=3{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ from $C$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 3-(-1)\\cdot (-5)}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that since $x=3{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-82599/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ee52fd3-6c79-5016-ade5-46e7bfbb557a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82599"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-113573/selection/a4c6038bd18e8036c8aca9d91aad6483cba7506371c6e8444169dbebeb7adf13" :answer/id #uuid "4411aeb9-ad19-5330-ac71-5cad4405e27a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113573/selection/aba1b22c7d2b7ae85a8a9cd039bec0abc31f6d192ca76509c8226104c6e81cc8" :answer/id #uuid "2ec6b23e-ea2f-5ecf-a209-4e6fb81c9c68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}28 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113573/selection/7dee067e8481e07ffc418a7351e272fb3148a55433f521598c1cd2747da2f63c" :answer/id #uuid "1ce2d6e2-f798-5844-b19f-24a867a1d05c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 42\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113573/selection/cc439d6ceaf8def401cdf92c2354024f9481f87582ac445b4373eec964efdd08" :answer/id #uuid "28ebc061-25b9-59ba-94f6-c87435e3473c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-16 \\\\ 26\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113573/selection/88c853e25cd7c43f0eb90e13f72f4add395e1c4d342a8f7292546262c0beb69e" :answer/id #uuid "6874fa14-0d02-5c30-