n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}28 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-113573/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ee52fd3-6c79-5016-ade5-46e7bfbb557a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-113573"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-82705/selection/9576b88f964aafa72109b0daf8e5011e1276983566a81ec66c0ae1d06856933c" :answer/id #uuid "0b9f4e4d-835d-55bb-9340-bbef4fe1694a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82705/selection/10b1e2f8a97f5e444dd5c20214eb6a23bf68bd785ad41aaafb9dbbacbfd32399" :answer/id #uuid "7d767114-2165-5418-815c-c5f6a31b28be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82705/selection/bcf965bd290e223b17dfdadc7b50fe8a18cfb34e6cd446742ad483581bda7281" :answer/id #uuid "256bafd9-8fa1-5fa4-b57b-08e9dd1f4a59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82705/selection/f4d383f82bff7b527921b93b850dbb8a4ec696f737408cb6ab2fb4b502ce71ad" :answer/id #uuid "d8dfcfcb-71e3-5654-be6c-354969d0dbcb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82705/selection/7d4b449c1763ac7fcb95922e8064b3210f1e4412b9fa8e29cb5b070bb32a0c76" :answer/id #uuid "ece2bb12-a445-5699-a1b3-4dfcdda1f733" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82705/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cf12b751-c51c-5fc0-90db-f298ee710324" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-82705/selection/f4d383f82bff7b527921b93b850dbb8a4ec696f737408cb6ab2fb4b502ce71ad" :answer-field/choices ["q-82705/selection/9576b88f964aafa72109b0daf8e5011e1276983566a81ec66c0ae1d06856933c" "q-82705/selection/10b1e2f8a97f5e444dd5c20214eb6a23bf68bd785ad41aaafb9dbbacbfd32399" "q-82705/selection/bcf965bd290e223b17dfdadc7b50fe8a18cfb34e6cd446742ad483581bda7281" "q-82705/selection/f4d383f82bff7b527921b93b850dbb8a4ec696f737408cb6ab2fb4b502ce71ad" "q-82705/selection/7d4b449c1763ac7fcb95922e8064b3210f1e4412b9fa8e29cb5b070bb32a0c76"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-82705" :question/id #uuid "aabb7d44-6631-59cb-8c14-d07df8ca4ee7" :question/math-academy-id "q-82705" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ to $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ is given below. Find $[x]_{B}$ given that $x=-3{c}_{1}-5{c}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ from $C$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 6-5\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}6 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that since $x=-3{c}_{1}-5{c}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-82705/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ee52fd3-6c79-5016-ade5-46e7bfbb557a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82705"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-36503"] :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $C$ are given below. What is $[x]_{B}?$ \n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ from $C$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot (-3)}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}22 \\\\ 35\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-36485/selection/5c85a896b26a63e24426473a495b51cc8d24cd536c398e4352b009cb02762104" :answer/id #uuid "ea153dcc-b309-539e-bc1b-3fef6ac3a406" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36485/selection/e9f231a693a7970fb2f031e5f039d263cf4f2934df16dce52b677ad0cc3c4555" :answer/id #uuid "25ccef5a-1140-55fe-aa99-9a26fe9a58ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}